# Physical melee (#39, D-038, D-NEW): a swing of the sword in the IK hand hits, its damage from the speed of the blade
# where it touched (#465; the damage scale itself is melee-damage.xrs); the trigger charges nothing and never starts the
# engine's strike while the IK hand holds the weapon.
# Runs on the test save mvp-goblin-fight (#70: a sword equipped, a goblin ahead in a corridor):
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence melee-swing -Save mvp-goblin-fight
# The swings are ramps of the simulated right controller: 0.85 m in 8 frames - 9.6 m/s at 90 fps, 3.2 m/s at 30 fps,
# above the swing speed (2.5 m/s) and below a tracking jump (20 m/s) at any frame rate the runner plays at. Every other
# move of the hand is a slow ramp too: an instant move is a tracking jump only on a short frame - the set-up's 0.43 m
# in one 22 ms frame (45 fps, a busy runner) is 19.5 m/s, a swing (#349, TRAPS.md).
@sim idle
@save mvp-goblin-fight
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
@assert vr.melee.active eq true
@assert vr.melee.placed eq true
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0

# The goblin held still 80 units ahead (the save has it walking away down the corridor), the sword level with its
# chest, the blade pointing ahead, the hand to the right - moved there slowly (0.43 m in 60 frames: under 0.7 m/s)
goblin_base_0036.setspeed 0
place goblin_base_0036 80
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
vr-sim head rot 0 -25 0
@frames 75
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0
@shot goblin-in-reach

# 1. A slow sweep through the goblin (0.85 m in 60 frames: under 1.3 m/s) is no swing and hits nothing
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 75
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 0

# 2. A swing back through it: one hit, its damage from the speed of the blade's point that touched
@mark
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 1 5s
@frames 30
@assert vr.melee.swinging eq false
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 1
@assert vr.melee.last.target eq goblin_base_0036
@assert vr.melee.last.aim gt 0.1
@assert vr.melee.last.speed gt 1.5
@log melee\.hit source=player target=goblin_base_0036 .*aim=\S+ speed=\S+ kind=(slash|thrust)
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=hit .*hits=1

# 3. The trigger held 2 s, then a swing: a hit like any other - the trigger charges nothing (#465)
@mark
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 180
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq true
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 2 5s
@frames 30
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 2
@assert vr.melee.last.aim gt 0.1
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 5
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq false
@nolog melee\.charge

# 6. The engine's own strike no longer starts from the trigger while the IK hand holds the weapon - also in the combat
# mode, where it used to strike without any animation (the owner's headset fight, 2026-10-10)
@mark
combat on
@until vr.weapon.combatMode eq true 5s
@frames 30
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 40
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq true
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 30
@nolog vr\.body\.armAnim.*strike
@nolog melee\.hit
combat off
@frames 30

# 7. A menu stops the swings: the inventory open, a fast sweep is no swing
ui inventory open
@until vr.melee.active eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.refused eq inventory
@remember swings vr.melee.swings
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 30
@assert vr.melee.swings eq {swings}
ui inventory close
@until vr.melee.active eq true 5s

@shot after-hits
@assert errors eq 0
